Simplify market listing cards + add listing detail modal

Task #5: Replace verbose market listing cards with clean minimal rows
and introduce a full ListingDetailModal for tapped listings.

Changes to app/(tabs)/market.tsx:
- ListingCard now shows only: card thumbnail, card name, seller name, price (or TRADE badge)
- All action buttons, description, photos, status badges, and external URL removed from card rows
- Tapping a listing opens ListingDetailModal (Modal with presentationStyle="pageSheet")
- Modal fetches card data using typed queryFn: () => fetchCard(listing.cardId), typed as useQuery<PokemonCard>
- Modal displays: large card image, card name, set name, card number + rarity, FOR SALE/TRADE badge,
  price, condition, seller name, description, moderation status banner (real owner only),
  external URL button, seller photos, action bar
- Split permission flags: isRealOwner (userId === currentUserId) for owner-only moderation banner;
  isOwner (passed from parent, includes staff) for delete; canReport (userId !== currentUserId) for report
  so staff can delete but still see report on other listings and moderation banner never shows for staff
- Delete closes modal before firing deleteListing(); Message closes modal then navigates
- No "last sold" or externally-sourced pricing shown anywhere
- Removed ActivityIndicator import (unused); added PokemonCard type import for proper typing
- No any-casts remain; card query result is properly typed as PokemonCard | undefined
- Added modalStyles stylesheet for the detail modal layout
